---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import LastVerified from '../../components/LastVerified.astro';
import UpdateBadge from '../../components/UpdateBadge.astro';
import QuickAnswer from '../../components/QuickAnswer.astro';
import SourceList from '../../components/SourceList.astro';
import AdsterraNativeBanner from '../../components/AdsterraNativeBanner.astro';
import AdsterraBanner300x250 from '../../components/AdsterraBanner300x250.astro';
import { sourceUrls, patch107, patch109, patch110, latestAppliedPatch, update110, update111, patch111, patch112, patch111Preview, update11Preview } from '../../data/sources';

const title = 'DragonSword Awakening Roadmap: Latest Updates & Future Plans';
const description = 'DragonSword Awakening update status: 1.1.1 is applied, 1.1.0 added Ryza, Hunt updates and the Training Ground, and later Hero dates remain unconfirmed.';
const canonical = 'https://dragonswordguide.com/roadmap/';
const article = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article', headline: title, description, mainEntityOfPage: canonical, datePublished: '2026-08-08', dateModified: '2026-10-22', publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'DragonSword Guide' } };
const sources = [
  { label: 'Official update notes 1.1.1', href: update111.href, note: 'Evidence B — final applied fixes; published October 15, 2026.' },
  { label: 'Official update notes 1.1.0', href: update110.href, note: 'Evidence B — final release notes; published October 15, 2026. Supersedes the earlier schedule.' },
  { label: 'Official LIVE STREAM #7 replay', href: update11Preview.replayHref, note: 'Evidence B — historical preview with English and Japanese captions; final 1.1.0 notes now establish release status.' },
  { label: 'Official 1.1 livestream notice', href: update11Preview.noticeHref, note: 'Evidence B — historical showcase announcement, retained as preview provenance.' },
  { label: 'Official Ryza teaser announcement', href: 'https://steamcommunity.com/games/4570720/announcements/detail/1844115010490208', note: 'Evidence B — published September 17, 2026 KST (September 16 UTC); announces her October arrival.' },
  { label: 'Official post-launch roadmap & Q&A', href: sourceUrls.roadmap, note: 'Evidence B — primary roadmap source for post-launch plans, heroes, Rifts, multiplayer Raids and platform status.' },
  { label: 'Official update notes 1.0.12', href: patch112.href, note: 'Evidence B — historical applied patch; published September 10, 2026 KST.' },
  { label: 'Official update notes 1.0.11', href: patch111.href, note: 'Evidence B — historical applied patch; published September 3, 2026 KST.' },
  { label: 'Official update notes 1.0.10', href: patch110.href, note: 'Evidence B — historical applied patch; published August 19, 2026.' },
  { label: 'Official 1.0.11 patch preview (historical)', href: patch111Preview.href, note: 'Evidence B — historical announcement source; its separate Coming Next items are not classified as applied 1.0.11 content.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} routeId="roadmap" ogType="article" schema={[article]}>
  <div class="shell page-wrap"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'DragonSword Guide', href: '/' }, { label: 'Roadmap' }]} /><article>
    <header class="article-header"><p class="eyebrow">Updates · Source timeline</p><h1>DragonSword Awakening Roadmap</h1><LastVerified date="October 22, 2026" /></header>
    <div class="roadmap-hero"><UpdateBadge label={`${latestAppliedPatch.label} · ${latestAppliedPatch.date}`} href={latestAppliedPatch.href} /><h2>Follow the official trail, not rumor.</h2><p>Update 1.1.1 is the latest applied patch confirmed by the official notes reviewed on October 22, 2026. Version 1.1.0 and its 1.1.1 fixes were released on October 15; the earlier schedule is now history.</p></div>
    <QuickAnswer title="Update 1.1.1 is applied; Version 1.1.0 is released."><p>Ryza, Hunt Rank and Hell Difficulty, the Training Ground and Othello Hero Quest were added in 1.1.0. Patch 1.1.1 fixes the reported quest and Hunt reward issues. Later Heroes still have no confirmed exact release dates in the sources reviewed here.</p></QuickAnswer>
    <AdsterraNativeBanner/>
    <div class="timeline"><div><span class="date">Latest applied / released</span><h2>1.1.1 applied</h2><p>October 15, 2026. The official notes confirm quest and Hunt reward fixes.</p></div><div><span class="date">Released / previous</span><h2>1.1.0 released</h2><p>October 15, 2026. Ryza, the Training Ground and Hunt additions are released.</p></div><div><span class="date">Later / date unknown</span><h2>Remaining Hero plans</h2><p>Jerome, Veronica and Logan remain plans without confirmed exact dates in the sources reviewed here.</p></div></div>
    <section class="roadmap-details"><h2>Latest applied / released: 1.1.1</h2><p>The final notes confirm fixes for Ryza leveling after Quest #53, the Reina conversation step in Quest #45, and Hunt reward currency. Hunt ranks, scores and rewards were reset as part of that fix; first-time rank rewards can be earned again.</p><h2>Released / previous: 1.1.0</h2><p>The final release notes replace the earlier October 15 preview as the source for applied status:</p><ul><li>Ryza (Playable Hero) — rewarded for Adventure Quest #53, “Reunion”; granted immediately if that quest was already completed.</li><li>Othello Hero Quest — added after Chapter 5.</li><li>Hunt Hell Difficulty — added alongside Hunt scores and ranks.</li><li>Training Ground — entered through Edric in front of Roderic Palace, with a stationary dummy or combat-active targets and damage/DPS readouts.</li><li>Quality-of-life changes include cooking Quick Slots increasing from two to three, additional map pin types, and Familiar acquisition through the Codex.</li></ul><p class="evidence-note"><strong>Release boundary:</strong> these are confirmed additions from the final 1.1.0 notes, not tested strategies or balance recommendations. Older preview details do not override the final notes.</p><h2>Release history: 1.0.12</h2><p>The official applied notes list these fixes:</p><ul><li>Localization corrections to Aria’s Bomb Arrows attack-count description and Theresia’s costume weapon description.</li><li>Astria’s Slide no longer receives an unintended cooldown after learning Blazing Lightning, and the hero can rotate while using Slide.</li><li>Fixes for abnormal Super Armor during Andras the Cave Predator’s ceiling-hanging pattern, unintended invincibility when switching coincides with a hit-induced Familiar dismount, and a 5-Star Equipment crafting result popup that could not be closed after the cinematic finished.</li></ul><h2>Release history: 1.0.11</h2><p>The final official Update Notes confirm these applied areas:</p><ul><li>Just Dodge, including its documented invincibility, guaranteed-critical, Active Skill Rage and Dodge Stamina effects.</li><li>Lock-On control, retention, target-search and camera improvements.</li><li>A one-second Super Armor protection for the Hero left on the field after switching.</li><li>Balance changes for Lute, Aria, Tarte, Roxy, Astria, Kalsion and Dana.</li><li>Multiplayer Retry, fastest-response lobby search, version notices, lobby fixes and departure notifications.</li><li>System quality-of-life work, localization corrections and listed bug fixes.</li></ul><p class="evidence-note"><strong>Final-notes boundary:</strong> these applied claims come from the final 1.0.11 Update Notes, not merely from the earlier preview.</p><h2>Release history: 1.0.10</h2><ul><li>Update 1.0.10 remains a historical applied release dated August 19, 2026.</li><li><a href={patch107.href}>1.0.7</a> remains historical context for Quick Entry, the former matching-range setting, map pins and Rune changes.</li></ul><h2>Later / date unknown</h2><ul><li>Earlier official roadmap material also names Jerome, Veronica and Logan as planned Heroes, alongside broader Hero Quest, Rift and multiplayer Raid direction. Their dependable release dates remain unknown.</li><li>The roadmap does not establish a current console launch date, cross-platform play or story/open-world co-op.</li></ul><p class="evidence-note"><strong>Evidence B boundary:</strong> the roadmap, official Steam announcements and official replay are primary sources. Community pages may help identify questions, but they do not upgrade a feature, date, platform or character claim.</p><AdsterraBanner300x250/><p>For current system changes, continue to the <a href="/systems/runes/">Rune guide</a> or the <a href="/builds/">build framework</a>; those pages own their narrower intents.</p></section>
    <SourceList sources={sources} />
  </article></div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.page-wrap{padding:1.25rem 0 2rem}.article-header{max-width:820px;margin-bottom:1.5rem}.eyebrow{color:var(--accent-light);font-size:.72rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase}h1,h2{line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.04em}h1{font-size:clamp(2.4rem,7vw,5rem);margin:0 0 .7rem}h2{font-size:clamp(1.45rem,3vw,2rem);margin:.8rem 0 .45rem}.roadmap-hero{padding:1.5rem;background:linear-gradient(115deg,var(--accent-soft),var(--paper));border:1px solid hsl(199 86% 58% / .35);border-radius:14px}.roadmap-hero p{max-width:60ch;color:var(--muted-strong)}.timeline{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1rem;margin:2.5rem 0}.timeline>div{border-top:1px solid var(--accent);padding-top:1rem}.timeline h2{margin:.35rem 0;font-size:1.3rem}.timeline p{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem}.date{color:var(--accent-light);font-size:.72rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em}@media(max-width:700px){.timeline{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
